    {
      "id": "2115148489873322036",
      "author": "elonmusk",
      "author_name": "Elon Musk",
      "author_avatar": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/2053244804520427520/m8mdWZCG_200x200.jpg",
      "author_verified": true,
      "author_verified_type": "individual",
      "created_at_utc": "2026-10-27T18:27:52.000Z",
      "created_at_shanghai": "2026-10-28 02:27:52",
      "type": "转发",
      "type_label": "转发",
      "text": "The sheer fucking hypocrisy surrounding Elon Musk is breathtaking.\n\nFor decades, billionaire-funded foundations have financed advocacy groups, political campaigns, legal organizations, and efforts to reshape public policy.\n\nGeorge Soros is one of the most prominent examples.\n\nAnd somehow that influence is routinely presented as enlightened philanthropy.\n\nThen Elon Musk enters politics, spends openly, challenges powerful institutions, and suddenly the entire establishment discovers the dangers of billionaire influence.\n\nGive me a fucking break.\n\nThe man has built companies that launch rockets, connect the world through satellites, manufacture vehicles, and advance technologies with enormous implications for humanity.\n\nHis long-term ambition is to make civilization multiplanetary.\n\nHe has a profound personal interest in a future where technological progress remains possible.\n\nYou can disagree with his politics.\n\nBut pretending he’s just another billionaire looking for influence ignores the extraordinary scale of what he’s actually trying to accomplish.",
      "quote": null,
      "retweet": {
        "author": "tslryn",
        "avatar": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/2105349594263486464/67SqeEuc_200x200.jpg",
        "created_at_shanghai": "2026-10-27 09:59:43",
        "created_at_utc": "2026-10-27T01:59:43.000Z",
        "id": "2114899814177480951",
        "images": [],
        "media": [],
        "name": "Ryan",
        "text": "The sheer fucking hypocrisy surrounding Elon Musk is breathtaking.\n\nFor decades, billionaire-funded foundations have financed advocacy groups, political campaigns, legal organizations, and efforts to reshape public policy.\n\nGeorge Soros is one of the most prominent examples.\n\nAnd somehow that influence is routinely presented as enlightened philanthropy.\n\nThen Elon Musk enters politics, spends openly, challenges powerful institutions, and suddenly the entire establishment discovers the dangers of billionaire influence.\n\nGive me a fucking break.\n\nThe man has built companies that launch rockets, connect the world through satellites, manufacture vehicles, and advance technologies with enormous implications for humanity.\n\nHis long-term ambition is to make civilization multiplanetary.\n\nHe has a profound personal interest in a future where technological progress remains possible.\n\nYou can disagree with his politics.\n\nBut pretending he’s just another billionaire looking for influence ignores the extraordinary scale of what he’s actually trying to accomplish.",
